; THE INVERSE ROUNDS  and nothing else; no schedule and no table;
;
; Entered at the block's own zero with THE CIPHERTEXT AT @0x0c0:0x0cf  the
; inverse table resident  the last round key in the regression window and the
; ten temps standing; It leaves the plaintext in the state at @0x0d3:0x0e2;
;
; block/aes128dsetup puts all of that there and its header says why the two
; are separate files at all;
;
; IT SPENDS WHAT IT IS GIVEN; the window is REGRESSED a word at a time down to
; the original key and the ten temps are consumed on the way  so a caller
; running a second block must restore both from a copy taken after the setup;
; Fifty six bytes; The alternative was to regenerate them  which cannot be
; done  because regenerating them needs the FORWARD table and that is the one
; thing the setup threw away;
;
; AND EVERYTHING ELSE IT NEEDS CLEAR  IT CHECKS; the two zero contracts below
; the clears are not decoration: they are what tells a mode that its restore
; set was too small  at the block that first reuses a dirty cell rather than
; three rounds later in a wrong byte; They were already here when this was one
; file  where they could only ever be true; here they do work;
;
; CONTRACTS ARE RELATIVE and the include's offset resolves them;
;
; TAPE MAP  (relative to the block's own zero)
;   @0x000        cnt
;   @0x053:0x056  scratch for the downward turn
;   @0x057:0x07e  the temp run{40}  SPENT
;   @0x07f:0x082  scratch for the upward turn
;   @0x083:0x09b  aes/xorword pasted at 131
;   @0x09c:0x09f  g{4}
;   @0x0a0:0x0af  window{16}  REGRESSING in place  down to the original key
;   @0x0b0:0x0bf  cleared below  it is phase one's leavings
;   @0x0c0:0x0cf  the ciphertext  which the caller puts here
;   @0x0d3:0x0e2  state{16}  the plaintext comes back here
;   @0x0e3:0x0f2  the round key
;   @0x0f3:0x3f5  the INVERSE table  read only here

; the ciphertext comes up to the state  where it stays
; sixteen bytes  nineteen cells
  R192[-R19+L19]L192R193[-R19+L19]L193R194[-R19+L19]L194R195[-R19+L19]L195
  R196[-R19+L19]L196R197[-R19+L19]L197R198[-R19+L19]L198R199[-R19+L19]L199
  R200[-R19+L19]L200R201[-R19+L19]L201R202[-R19+L19]L202R203[-R19+L19]L203
  R204[-R19+L19]L204R205[-R19+L19]L205R206[-R19+L19]L206R207[-R19+L19]L207
; the window and the round constant fall inside phase two's
; frames  and both still hold something  so both are cleared
; clear
  R176[-]L176R177[-]L177R178[-]L178R179[-]L179R180[-]L180R181[-]L181
  R182[-]L182R183[-]L183R184[-]L184R185[-]L185R186[-]L186R187[-]L187
  R188[-]L188R189[-]L189R190[-]L190R191[-]L191R237[-]L237
; ASSERT ptr=+0
; ASSERT zero +176:+210
; ASSERT zero +227:+242

; ==== phase two : the inverse rounds ====
; the LAST round key first  which is what makes this the inverse
; the round key is COPIED beside the state  and NOT moved; the committed cut
; moved it  which was right there because w{176} held every round key and
; none was wanted twice; here the window IS wanted again  as the next
; regression's input  so a move would destroy the schedule;
  R160[-R67+L71+R4]L160R156[-R4+L4]L156R161[-R67+L72+R5]L161R156[-R5+L5]L156
  R162[-R67+L73+R6]L162R156[-R6+L6]L156R163[-R67+L74+R7]L163R156[-R7+L7]L156
